  "body": "## What changed\nSTEP imports now meter B-spline, NURBS and pcurve edge subdivisions.\nExtrusions and revolutions use the same guarded curve division.\nA refused edge names its position and shell.\nA refused swept generator names its face through the existing meter.\nHealthy divisions keep truck's probes, order and output.\n\n## Cause\nEdge curves and swept generators bypassed the surface evaluation guard.\nZero-weight rational curves exceeded a 20-second test barrier.\nA discontinuous B-spline could also pass at a coarse tolerance.\n\n## Tests\nThe first four pins failed on unchanged upstream code and passed after the fix:\n- `discontinuous_edge_curve_is_refused_by_name`\n- `discontinuous_swept_curve_is_refused_by_name`\n- `zero_weight_edge_curve_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_zero_weight_swept_curve_division_is_bounded_and_trips`\n\nAdditional pins cover the evaluation budget, non-finite probes, invalid arguments, unresolved leaves, coarse-tolerance jumps and safe revolution fallback.\nExact comparisons cover healthy B-spline and NURBS divisions, extrusions, and transformed and reversed revolutions.\nJoined full-multiplicity knots and trims away from jumps remain accepted.\n\nRestoring upstream production code made all four original pins fail again.\nSix isolated mutations also failed their targeted pins: finite-probe check, evaluation charging, argument validation, unresolved-leaf refusal, revolution fallback and knot-jump check.\nAll restored pins passed.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on the first run.\nIt ran app unit tests and 18 mapped import suites with no failures.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` was empty.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe release heavy lane and the full external STEP corpus were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\nNo open PR changes the touched files.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Refuse runaway or discontinuous STEP edge and swept-curve subdivisions by name while preserving healthy division output.\n\nFixes #1545\n",
